The Dove Bank Ltd database is normalised to Third Normal Form (3NF) to reduce data duplication and maintain data consistency.

First Normal Form (1NF)
Each column contains only one value, and each record is uniquely identified by a primary key.

For example, each customer has one customer ID, and customer details such as first name, last name, email and phone number are stored in separate fields.

Second Normal Form (2NF)
The database is in 2NF because each table has a primary key, and the information in each table depends on that primary key.

For example, the account number, account type and balance depend on the account ID.

Third Normal Form (3NF)
The database is in 3NF because customer, account and transaction information are stored in separate tables.

This reduces duplication. Customer details are stored in CUSTOMERS, account details in ACCOUNTS, and transaction details in TRANSACTIONS.
